From: James Livingston <jwl@ntmail.zso.dec.com>
Subject: RE: clinear error message

Mitch,

The Clinear port overlay message is a bug in the clinear.sys driver, and
is benign, but it will go away with Windows NT version 4.0.  You cannot,
alas, make the display faster; the chip is a very modest performer, and
its best is what you see. As long as you're running 3.51, you must use
clinear.sys and framebuf.dll.  With version 4.0 you can choose between
that and  vga.sys/vga.dll.  Our observation is that, under version 4.0,
vga.sys is marginally faster than clinear.sys.  If you want a faster
display, pick up an ISA or PCI display controller; almost any
currently-shipping model will be an improvement over the Cirrus Logic
Linear 5422 chip.

Cheers,
James

P.S.  Aaron, you might want to put a note on this AlphaServer 1000
baseboard VGA matter in the FAQ, eh?

