Hi Joel,

This product is the "old" (my, how computer technology compresses time!)
WorkGroup Web Forum product.  It received *RAVE* reviews in PC Week a month
or so ago.  It is a *very* nifty tool, in that it provides workgroup
collaboration in a WAN environment (inter- or intra-net), multimedia support,
plus no client licensing costs, utilizing a standard Web browser.  Since
the product is server based, the majority of the functionality is as portable
as your Web browser.

If you've got PATHWORKS 6.0, you've got it's little brother included, the
WorkGroup Web (WGWeb, or now, "AltaVista LAN Browser").  This is a client
based extension to a standard Web browser (you get a helper app that works
via a network drive connection pointing to your .WBL and .HTM files).  Slow
on an AXP 150, but still usable enough for me to manage a site full of PW
users.

Last I'd heard (before the name change, anyways), it was about $1K for the
Forum product, and $80 per seat for the LAN Browser.  We are looking at the
Forum product now to replace the LAN Browser (our company is geographically
disperse, and we've had moderate success with WGWeb in the local office).

