From: Gilbert Armour <garmour@minnie.hollins.edu>
Subject: RE: Mixing client->server & server->printer protocols

Yes, you can use different protocols in getting the print job to the print 
device.  What is the protocol for your network?  If your're using TCP/IP 
you can give the HP5 an IP address and use LPR to print to it.  If your're 
using AT then again print to the HP5 using AT.  If you're using NetBUEI, 
then I'd suggent DLC to the printer.  I would keep the number of protocols 
down to a minimum because each protocol takes server and bandwidth 
resources.

BTW, we have HPs with IP addresses being printed to from three different 
servers and parallel ports.  THe HP handles all inputs very well, as long 
as all  sources have small numbers of jobs.  Don't worry if both VMS and NT 
have PQs for the HP5.  It'll handle it whichever is easir for you to 
administer and set up.

