Abhay,
 
  You can get away with crossover 10baseT patch cables between two machines,
but I don't think that will work for three machines.  You need a hub to
bounce the signals between the three ports.  

  Hubs don't have to cost a lot - I picked up a 4 port 10baseT hub at the
local superstore (Fry's Electronics, Sunnyvale) for about $40.  Made by
LinkSys. It's about the size of a pack of cigarettes.  Works fine between my
P120 and AlphaStation.  One advantage of having a hub is the
transmit/receive lights - so you can diagnose problems, or just see what's
going on between the machines.

-Danny Thorpe
