I know we have done it with three intel boxes.. one with NT (as the 
router basically) and the other two with Win95.  However, we only did 
it while we were waiting for our hub.

I am assuming that you have the cables twisted properly and that you 
also have the cards all set up for RJ-45.  Assuming that, you 
shouldn't have a whole lot of trouble.  I don't recall having much of 
a hassle with it.  We were running winnt 3.5 but are now running nt 
4.0 and 3.51 (mainly) with RJ-45 network.  I don't recall what our 
last hub cost us but I don't think that it was a whole lot.  I know 
our switched hubs cost quite a bit but that is not something that you 
need.

Your best bet is to either run thinnet/coax (BNC) or purchase a HUB.  
The cost is not much more than a half decent nic.  

Anyways, good luck with which ever option you take!
Bernie
 
