You can use any PPP dialer from WFW to access IP services through a RAS 
server. (Spry's Ibox, Chamelion, etc.)  Unfortunately, this will provide 
only basic IP connectivity such as FTP, Telnet, or Web access, and will not 
allow Netbios over IP which is what you'll need to connect to an NT File or
Print share.  So, basically you'll have to dial in twice,  once using 
RAS/Netbuei to access file and print shares, and once via PPP to access 
TCP/IP resources.  

