DHCP and DNS have no connection between them.  I suggest you also install 
WINS which ties computer netbios names to IP addresses.  This is a dynamic 
data base and changes as the mapping changes.  DNS only works for static IP 
addresses like you server and routers.  Besides, it is manually managed and 
cannot keep up with the IP address changes of DHCP.

