Subject: FW: Command Scheduler Owner

This should work in much the same way as replication.
You need a "dummy" user account.  Give this acct the
appropriate rights - BackupOp, and set the password to
never expire and give it something you'll REMEMBER!.
  Then under Control Panel / Services  select Scheduler 
[which is the AT command].  Select Startup & use this 
account to log in as a service.

That should do it, however, just like replication you may need
to do that Unix-like thing and stop and restart the service
before it'll work

