owner-alphant wrote:
>Is there a way to specify a directory of the form %HOMEDRIVE%%HOMEPATH%   
for
>the FTP server directory? When I do it, FTP rejects connection with the
>'invalid directory' message. I would like to be able to have FTP users   
connect
>to their own directory, if possible, rather than a hard-coded one.
>
>Can it be done?
>
>thanks,
>
>Nik Zapantis

This functionality is in v4.0.  We (the mail list) recently went through   
some discussion around this and came to the conclusion that the next best   
thing that could be done with 3.51 was to set the default to one level   
above all the user accounts:

 FTP server dir
  |
   ------+--------+--------+--------+-- -  -
               /pub     /user1   /user2   /user3 ...

Then, when someone logs in, they can go to the pub dir or a specific user   
dir.  If the server dir is set up on an  NTFS partition, you'll be able   
to protect the individual's directories accordingly.

Sorry.

Aaron
