Subject: NT 4.0 Radical Suggestion

Hello everyone - I received from a friend a copy of Win NT 4.0 Beta 
     for my DEC ALpha Station 200 4/233. I was real excited to install it 
     because the 486 emulation included in it will allow me to run some 
     software that I have not gotten to run or didn't have a DEC Alpha 
     version of, like Netscape 2.0 and Corel Photopaint 5.0. 
        My radical suggestion to all the DEC & Microsoft people on this 
     list is this: why doesn't DEC and Microsoft just post the beta of Win 
     NT 4.0, Alpha version (and other non-intel platforms too)? It seems 
     that all non-intel platforms that run NT will buy the product. Letting 
     them download the beta for evaluation will allow them to use the 
     emulation and Win 95 interface until the product is shipped, which 
     seems to be slipped every time it's announced. And Microsoft 
     practically gives it away now anyway, so what why not post it for the 
     individuals like me that can't make it on the eval team or attend an 
     NT Con meeting?
        Well, that's my two cents. Before I get off my sopbox, though, has 
     anyone who has NT 4.0 and is using Netscape 2.0X ever get to use the 
     VRML stuff? Thanks in advance.
     
     Steve Schelfhout
     Schelfhout_Steve@ccmail.ncsc.navy.mil

