Steve,

There is one sure reason that they distribute it on CD and not via
net-download - SIZE !!!

Considering what NT is, I would say the files involved may be of the order
of 30+ Mb in size even when compressed (not actually having NT yet I'm
guessing, but hey, Win3.11 was 7 or 8 disks at least way back then).  That's
one very long FTP transfer and would sure slow any site down because of
bandwidth hassles, number of concurrent FTP users exceeded, not to mention
FTP drop-outs from time to time.  If they sent 200,000 CDs out as beta's,
imagine all 200,000 trying to access an FTP site, even over the space of a
month, and downloading the beta.  It would be totally unacceptable.

Secondly, CDs are portable and so you don't have to have a spare hard disk
with the NT 4.0 beta kit on it, since you may/may-not be able to use it off
an existing NT 3.51 file system (just a guess).

For a few bucks to produce and ship the CD, that's probably a lot less cost
than all those net accesses too.

FWIW, my $0.02 in reply

