What all NT Backup products fail to provide is a function similar to 
Standalone Backup in VMS.  The lack of this capability makes it harder 
than it should be to restore a failed system partition on NT.  Yes you 
can play around with recovery disks, registry restores, etc.,  but after 
having to perform a handful of system partition restores,  it never goes 
smoothly and most of the time you end up completely re-installing NT.  

Why can't one of the backup manufacturers create a subset of their 
application on bootable floppies that contains NTFS, FAT, CD, and Tape
drivers and that will bring a system up just enough to restore data without 
worrying about contention with open operating system files?????

Boy do I miss standalone backup.

