From jwl@ntmail.zso.dec.com Tue Jun 18 19:12:22 1996 CDT
Message-ID: <c=US%a=_%p=Digital%l=NTMAIL2-960618165946Z-9811@ntmail3.zso.dec.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Jun 1996 09:59:46 -0700
From: James Livingston <jwl@ntmail.zso.dec.com>
Subject: FW: making a VMS system become an NT box

Dan,

Rich is dead right about getting the correct firmware, and about the
partitions other than your system partition being formatted with NTFS.

However, you should probably make a six-MByte FAT system partition, and
make it the second partition on your system disk; six Mbytes is better
than a smaller number, because it enables you to support more than one
release on the same system partition, a good safety strategy.  Also, if
you make this partition the second of two, which is our
factory-installed software default, you give those installation programs
that insist on targeting C: a chance of success.  That's why we chose
that convention in the first place.

Be sure to get the latest firmware from our Web page, 

    http://www.windowsnt.dec.com/default.htm.  

Look for the product name, after selecting the "Drivers & Firmware"
link.

Cheers,
James
