From: Danny Thorpe <dthorpe@subliminal.com>
Subject: Re: NT 3.51 Filecompression

Tony,

  File compression is transparent - applications running on the NT machine
don't know that some or all of the files in a directory are compressed, and
other machines that access those files through shares certainly don't know
how they are physically stored.

  You probably got the "No files" message because network access rights are
disabled on the server machine, or the remote userid doesn't have rights to
the NTFS partition or directory.  

  Win NT 3.50, WFW 3.11, Win 95, and anything else that can access NT shares
can access NTFS compressed files in those shares.

-Danny

