From: Andrew C Jakubczak <ajakubcz@facstaff.wisc.edu>
Subject: Printing Oddities

Hello All,

Got one for you. We run an Alpha w/ 3.51 and am sharing 2 Digital
Printserver 17s. Attached to this fine equipment are 4 labs whose machines
(Windows for Workgroups) log into a single Domain under 4 dummy accounts.
That is all the machines in a given lab will log in using the same username
and blank password.

The problem I'm encountering is that the queue does not remove (delete)jobs
after they run through the printer. (Yes, I have checked the box "delete
printed jobs.") Oddly enough, printing hasn't been better. On the WFW nodes,
the finished jobs just keep collecting indicating little if anything about
their status. In Print manager on the server, the jobs also collect and they
show up as 'printed'.

This seems to only happen to accounts with blank passwords. Other user
accounts drop out of the queue as expected. 

I know what your going to say. "Add passwords you big dope!" Well, I can't
at this time. Have any of you seen such behavior?

Sincerely,

Andy

