Angelo,

I've written a Windows NT print spooler for the Epson Stylus Colour 
printer which *should* (no guarantees until I've tried it) allow you to 
do something along the lines of what you want to do.  Essentially all 
it does it pretend it's a printer (over AppleTalk, because it's for 
Macs, not PCs), and forwards anything sent to it to the NT print 
spooler.  The file then gets printed without NT's drivers getting in 
the road.

If you don't have any success finding an alternate solution, I don't 
think it'll be too serious a problem to change my AppleTalk interface 
to a TCP/IP sockets or Microsoft Network interface.  Then you'll just 
need to be careful about what you send to the printer.

Phil.

