	Jim,

		Thanks for the input. You confirmed what we had feared.

		Your answer, however, begs the questions: Has anyone come
	up with a seamless solution to this? Are there any third-party
	suppliers that offer this functionality (ie selecting PS or ANSI
	or PCL, etc) when printing? And finally, how long and at what 
	price could something like this be developed? I am having difficulty
	accepting that this is not a somewhat common problem.

		It is critical to the business that we integrate this print
	capability into the application. In other words, having production 
	print personnel using copy from DOS or using a DOS print command is 
	not an option in this environment. We are working with the SW vendor
	on seeking a solution also, as this criteria was discussed at
	length, during negotiations, and was described as quite easily
	implemented. The hardware vendors are getting pulled into this
	as well, as these vendors offer software for their printers,
	on other platforms, that gives this functionality.

		Even if the SW/HW vendors come through, I would still
	be interested in other offerings (if any) to see which is truly
	to most fully-functioned.

	Again, any and all assistance is greatly appreciated...Angelo

		

