-------------------------------------------------------------

MecDesign V2.5 - THE mechanical application
===========================================

Due  to  international sales & marketing, there are currently two names
used - "MecDesign" (International) and "MekPak" (Finland).

MecDesign  brings  powerful yet friendly, MicroStation-like ease of use
to the MicroStation  mechanicalengineering community. Unlike mechanical
drafting packages  that  have  been translated from lesser CAD systems,
MecDesign was designed from the  ground  up  as a MicroStation product.
MecDesign  combines  the  full  power  and  elegance  of MicroStation's
intuitive  user  interface  with  an  extensive  mechanical engineering
feature set. The result is that you'll become productive with MecDesign
virtually from the minute you first  start using it. With MecDesign you
don't just place lines and  circles in  a  design  file.  You  assemble
intelligent  CAD components into design files. Instead of creating each
component from a fixed, unchanging cell whose only adjustable parameter
is its scale,  MecDesign creates most components (like bolts and beams)
parametrically as you  built  your  design  file.  With  it's  advanced
features   like  automatic  control  for  drawing  scales  and  sheets,
automatically  updated  detailing  and  intelligent  bill  of materials
functions it simply gives you more time for real designing.

* Intelligent user interface		  * Associative dimensioning
* Drawing scale management		  * Multilingual support
* Support for most common standards	  * Flexible licensing
* Dynamic annotations on any element	  * Easy to configure
* Parametric and dynamic components	  * Advanced bill of materials
* Component data can be modified	  * Automated plotting software
* Automatically updated detailing	  * Modeler compatible
* File management utility with preview
* No need for external database

MecDesign - Advanced features
-----------------------------

Because  MecDesign   was  first  developed  to  MicroStation  V4 (which
introduced MDL) there are  no user-commands functions used. Application
development has always followed our main rule: the end-user must always
have full control to the design. That is made possible with dynamic and
parametric tools (instead of using hundreds of  cell libraries). To the
most common components (i.e. bolts and beams) bill of materials data is
automatically included  when the  component is  placed.  When  creating
material lists,  end-user  can  fully  define the looks and even create
different  sets. All  the  MecDesign  annotations can  be  edited  with
standard  MicroStation  or PowerDraft tools without MecDesign. The file
management utility with a 2D/3D- preview possibilities user  can easily
create and maintain project data (i.e. file descriptions, full  path to
the design file, notes and revisions etc.). With the plotting tool user
can simultaneously get access to all local or network printers/plotters
and even print several copies.

User-friendliness
-----------------

It is  obvious  that  one  application can not contain all the standard
components needed. So in MecDesign user can  modify  component data and
the changes  effect  also to  the  bill of materials. When a parametric
component is not available, we use intelligent cell-libraries: user can
change   cell  symbology  (all  element  attributes), select  different
projections  (all  that  dynamically before  placing the cell) and even
add their own cell libraries to MecDesign. MecDesign can be easily used
and configured as a network version too, so all the settings can reside
on the server and  every  client  workstation automatically uses  those
pre-defined configurations.

Productivity
------------
When working with  MecDesign  the  built-in  intelligence automatically
takes care about drawing sheets and scales, component data for material
lists, updating details, element symbology etc. This means that You are
in control!

MecDesign will run  on  most  MicroStation  and MicroStation PowerDraft
platforms. No need for external database.

