I doubt that you really have a DE101 -- they are very old and were 
never supported with Windows NT.  What I speculate that you really have 
(which is normal for Alpha 2100 systems) is an on-board DC21040 
adapter, going to a distribution panel which is (erroneously) labeled 
DE101.  I further expect that there is no blue jumper block on the 
Ethernet card, as there would be no Ethernet card at all.

	If this is all the case, then load the correct driver, and all should 
be well.  The correct driver is apparent in the V3.51 CD, under Digital 
and DC21040.  The version on the V3.5 CD was more difficult to locate, 
and is now out of date.

