From zeranski@ricks.enet.dec.com Mon Jun 24 14:32:42 1996 CDT
Message-ID: <9606241853.AA07856@easynet.crl.dec.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Jun 96 15:15:11 EDT
From: Beth Z. <zeranski@ricks.enet.dec.com>
Subject: RE: EB164 PCI IRQ problems

David,
       Although it is not intuitively obvious, ISA IRQ 3 and 4 do 
not conflict with PCI IRQ 3 and 4. All ISA device interrupts,
ie serial ports, LPT, IDE and floppy are routed through the
PIC (programmable interrupt controller) in the 82378 PCI-to-ISA
bridge.  The PCI interrupts are controlled through physically separate 
logic which is why having the same IRQ's is not a problem. 

       There is not enough information in your message to understand
why the video is not performing up to snuff. It could be a number
of issues. If WNT is using the generic VGA driver instead of the
driver for the #9gxe64pro then that's a likely problem that's
easy to fix.
 
