From:	CRL::"sp0t@promised-land.ai.mit.edu" "sp0t the w0nder slug" 21-JUN-1996 04:00:52.50
To:	alphant@garply.com
CC:	
Subj:	EB164 PCI IRQ problems

	Does anyone have any experience with 'reserving' IRQ's for use by 
the PCI Bus? I know you can do this in the BIOS of many Intel machines. 
The reason is, The SCSI controller (a qlogic in PCI slot 1) and the 
Ethernet (cogent em960 in PCI slot2) are taking IRQ's 4 and 3 
respectively, this as you can probably imagine is a bit of a problem due 
to the fact that IRQ's 3 and 4 are used by the serial ports.. PCI slot 2 
is IRQ 2 and PCI slot 1 is IRQ 1 which also can't be too good. Our video 
card (a #9gxe64pro in PCI slot 4) is not performing nearly as well as it 
should be expected to, video, including things as simple as the OpenGL 
screensavers are EXTREMELY choppy. Any information would be greatly 
appreciated...

---
