Abhay,

It sounds as if you're experiencing a SCSI termination problem.  Has
anything been changed recently, as in just before you began experiencing
your problems?  It's especially suggestive that you can get to your
small disk if the big one isn't connected to the SCSI adapter.

You're right, by the way, that any disk not seen during Windows NT's
boot sequence will never be seen by it - removable volumes excepted, of
course.

