Date: Thu, 27 Jun 1996 07:17:08 +0200
From: Tony Wilhelmsson <atotowi@ato.abb.se>
Subject: Re: Making VMS Alpha become an NT Alpha

Daniel A. Monjar wrote:
> 
> In any case, I have an Alpha 1000 4/200 that is currently running VMS.  I want to make it a NT box.  Does a
> standard NT install CD have everything I need to make this happen?  My biggest concern is how to make the 2+ MB
> FAT partition I will need.  Is there an Alpha NT version of FDISK?

 If your firmware is up to date all that you need to install WNT is on the WNT-CD. To create the 2+ MB 
FAT partition you'll have to run the ARCINST.EXE from the CD-ROM. To do this you choose the "Run a 
program" option from the ARC Boot-menu. The command line looks something like this:
scsi(X)cdrom(y)fdisk(0)\alpha\arcinst
To be sur to type the right numbers x,y check the hardware configuration in the ARC Supplementary menu 
for the adress to the CDROM. This programs asks if you would like to create a system partition and how 
many MB's it should be and then format it for you.
After this you run the Install WNT from CDROM option in the ARC Supplementary menu. Just follow the 
instructins.
