From: Greble, John H. <John.Greble@alcoa.com>
Subject: SMS and deleting records

Really and SMS question, but just in case someone my have an answer...

We are currently rolling out an SMS Hierarchy which calls for 
perhaps as many as 4 levels.  That is a site server reports to
another site server which reports to a hub and finally to
a central site.

We have been blissfully deleting records from all levels of the
hierarchy thinking that these deletes propagated to the other
servers in the chain.  After some confusing information from MS,
we did some testing and confirmed that deletes do NOT propagate.

Therefore I would like to know if other people are aware of this
'feature' and how they are handling it.  We are headed towards 100+
servers and 16k clients so this will be a major problem for us.
Adding to the problem is that we have out sourced the management
of the upper levels so that different people will care for the
data at different levels.  Anybody else see this as a major
problem?  If so what are you doing to work around?

Thanks!

